---
import LearningLayout from '../../../layouts/LearningLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import { confidenceProfile, foodSyntheses } from '../../../lib/food-evidence';
---
<LearningLayout title="What would support confidence in this finding?" section="confidence" intro="An outcome-level assessment should explain its judgements. It should not be calculated from a document count, a filter selection or a statistically significant result.">
  <div class="confidence-overview"><div><p class="eyebrow">Overall certainty</p><h2>Not assigned</h2><span class="status-pill">Demonstration profile only</span></div><p>The table illustrates domains a review team would consider for the four-week purchasing outcome. It is not a completed GRADE assessment: the data are fictional and several judgements are incomplete.</p></div>
  <div class="data-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Confidence assessment domains table"><table class="learning-table confidence-table"><caption>Illustrative assessment domains for the body of evidence, not scores for individual documents</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Domain</th><th scope="col">Example judgement</th><th scope="col">Reason or outstanding work</th></tr></thead><tbody>{confidenceProfile.map(item=><tr><th scope="row">{item.domain}</th><td>{item.judgement}</td><td>{item.reason}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <section class="learning-two-col learning-section"><div><h2>A sensitivity analysis answers a narrower question.</h2><p>Removing the high-risk fictional trial changes the pooled risk ratio from {foodSyntheses[0].rr.toFixed(2)} to {foodSyntheses[1].rr.toFixed(2)}. It does not automatically upgrade certainty or resolve reporting bias, indirectness or missing outcomes.</p><a class="text-link" href="/learning/food-access/effects/">Compare the two analyses <Icon/></a></div><div class="boundary-card"><h3>Qualitative findings need a separate approach</h3><p>Where appropriate, CERQual considers methodological limitations, coherence, adequacy and relevance for a qualitative synthesis finding. It is not a numerical rating of a community’s experience.</p><p>No CERQual assessment has been carried out on the invented materials in this demo.</p><a class="text-link" href="/learning/food-access/context/">Read the context examples <Icon/></a></div></section>
  <div class="learning-notice"><Icon name="info"/><div><strong>Guidance, not endorsement</strong><p>The display draws on the structure of <a href="https://www.cochrane.org/authors/handbooks-and-manuals/handbook/current/chapter-14">GRADE guidance</a> and <a href="https://www.cerqual.org/what-is-the-grade-cerqual-approach2/">CERQual</a>. Neither framework validates fabricated studies or supplies an automatic quality score.</p></div></div>
</LearningLayout>
